# Logging — read by log/logger.py
# LOG_LEVEL: DEBUG | INFO | WARNING | ERROR   (defaults to INFO)
LOG_LEVEL
# LOG_FILE_PATH: where the JSON log file is written for Grafana Alloy to tail.
# Leave empty to disable file logging and keep terminal output only.
# e.g. logs/app.log
LOG_FILE_PATH
# Loki — NOT read by the app, and not needed here at all. Grafana Alloy reads
# its own config file (config.alloy) and never looks at .env; the destination is
# set there. Documented only so it's obvious where logs go:
#   local dev + self-hosted VPS -> http://localhost:3100/loki/api/v1/push
#                                  (no credentials; Loki binds to localhost)
# If a Grafana Cloud endpoint is ever used instead, it additionally needs a
# numeric instance ID and an Access Policy token with the logs:write scope,
# passed as basic_auth in config.alloy — never committed here.
